{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+, Anti-MRSA", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Bridge", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is most similar (90%) to Plectasin C: 17%, G: 19%, K: 14%. Residues N5G6 and D11D12 were deleted from plectasin. Activity: active against Gram+ S. aureus ATCC 43300 or ATCC25923 or CVCC546 or E48 (MIC 4-16 ug/ml), S. epidermidis ATCC35984 or ATCC12228 (MIC 2-4 ug/ml), S. dysgalactiae CVCC3938 (MIC 4 ug/ml), S. agalactiae ATCC13813 or CAU-FRI-2022-01 or CAU-FRI-2022-02 (MIC 2-4 ug/ml), Gram- E.coli (MIC > 128 ug/ml), Shigella CMCC392 (MIC > 128 ug/ml), S.enteriditis CVCC3377 (MIC > 128 ug/ml), P.aeruginsoa CICC21630 (MIC > 128 ug/ml), and C.albicans (MIC >128 ug/ml). In vitro Toxicity: murine RBC: not hemo.lytic at 256 ug/ml. Recombinant production:yeast:Pichia pastoris: X33 strain, pPICZaA plasmid, 4 colonies expression level 137-203 mg/L. expressed supernatant was used for activity screen.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "38188573", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Front Microbiol. 2023 Dec 21;14:1304825. doi: 10.3389/fmicb.2023.1304825. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP04245", "source_id": "AP04245", "source_numeric_id": "04245", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP04245", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Plectasin: from evolution to truncation, expression, and better druggability.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
